# {{project_name}} — SPRAG Labs

A showcase app that exercises SPRAG's framework primitives one
entry at a time. Each route is a focused demonstration of a single
Specter + Ragot feature, runnable in isolation.

The labs skeleton is a living regression canary: every entry that
scaffolds + builds + renders cleanly proves the primitive still
works end-to-end. Adding a new entry is the easiest way to stress
a specific slice of the framework.

## Running

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
. .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
sprag dev --port 8000
```

Open <http://127.0.0.1:8000/>.

## Entries

| Route              | Mode     | What it exercises                          |
|--------------------|----------|--------------------------------------------|
| `/`                | document | Landing — links to every entry             |
| `/counter`         | hybrid   | `@action` + `Module` + `Component` loop    |
| `/virtual-scroll`  | hybrid   | `@virtual_scroll` on a large list          |
| `/store-demo`      | hybrid   | `store(...)` as cross-runtime shared state |

More entries (queue, watcher, operation, socket, model, animation)
are planned follow-ups — each is a forcing function for one gap.
